  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K K Chandri vs Azhiyur Grama Panchayath on 26 November, 2019 Author: Devan Ramachandran Bench: Devan Ramachandran In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Devan Ramachandran Tuesday, The 26Th Day Of November 2019 / 5Th Agrahayana, 1941 WP(C).No.24000 Of 2015(Y) Petitioner/S: K K Chandri, Aged 52 Years, D/O.Late Kelappan, Business, Residing At Kooteri House, Kuneemmal, Po Chombala-673 308 Vatakara, Kozhikode District. By Adv. Sri.R.Surendran Respondent/S: 1 Azhiyur Grama Panchayath, Azhiyur Kozhikode District, Represented By The Secretary, Azhiyur Grama Panchayat, Po Azhiyur, Pin-673 308, Kozhikode District. 2 The Secretary, Azhiyur Grama Panchayat, Po Azhiyur, Pin-673 308, Kozhikode District.",
    "facts": "2 I am considering these two Writ Petitions together because the petitioner in both these cases is the same and the reliefs sought for therein, though not dependent on each other, are edificed on similar factual circumstances. 2. Both these Writ Petitions have been filed by Smt.K.K.Chadri, who alleges that the Panchayath is now attempting to evict her from the shop room leased out to her in the year 2013, without following law and in violation of the applicable Statutes and Regulations. 3. WP(C)No.24000/2015 has been filed by the petitioner impugning Ext.P10 decision taken by the Panchayath, as per which, its Secretary has informed her that they have decided to evict her from the shop room and to re-allot it to others through a public auction. She says that Ext.P10 is untenable and that the Panchayath could not have taken such a decision WPC 24000/15 & 26043/19 because she can be evicted only as per the applicable Civil Law. 4. WP(C)No.26043//2019 was subsequently filed when the petitioner received Ext.P3 notice, as per which, she was asked to demolish certain alleged unauthorised constructions made to the shop room and she says that the allegations in this notice are untenable and without factual basis.",
    "arguments": "She, therefore, prays that the said notice be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and she be allowed to continue with the occupation of the shop room without interdiction from the Panchayath. 5. In response, Sri.R.Parthasarathy, learned Standing Counsel for the Azhiyur Grama Panchayath, submits that Ext.P10 in WP(C)No.24000/2015 is only a decision taken by the Panchayath to evict the petitioner in terms of law and to re-allot the shop room to others. He says that the petitioner could not have WPC 24000/15 & 26043/19 challenged this decision because she cannot assert that no action be taken to evict her in terms of law or that the Panchayath cannot re- allot the shop room to other persons. He, therefore, prays that liberty may be granted to his client to take appropriate action pursuant to Ext.P10 as per law. 6. Coming to Ext.P3 in WP(C)No.26043/2019, Sri.Parthasarthay submits that the said notice is only one issued under Section 235W of the Kerala Panchayath Raj Act ((herein after referred to as 'the Act' for short) and that the petitioner can always answer the same, thus leading to a final order to be issued by the Secretary in terms of law.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "She, therefore, prays that the said notice be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and she be allowed to continue with the occupation of the shop room without interdiction from the Panchayath. 5. In response, Sri.R.Parthasarathy, learned Standing Counsel for the Azhiyur Grama Panchayath, submits that Ext.P10 in WP(C)No.24000/2015 is only a decision taken by the Panchayath to evict the petitioner in terms of law and to re-allot the shop room to others. He says that the petitioner could not have WPC 24000/15 & 26043/19 challenged this decision because she cannot assert that no action be taken to evict her in terms of law or that the Panchayath cannot re- allot the shop room to other persons. He, therefore, prays that liberty may be granted to his client to take appropriate action pursuant to Ext.P10 as per law. 6. Coming to Ext.P3 in WP(C)No.26043/2019, Sri.Parthasarthay submits that the said notice is only one issued under Section 235W of the Kerala Panchayath Raj Act ((herein after referred to as 'the Act' for short) and that the petitioner can always answer the same, thus leading to a final order to be issued by the Secretary in terms of law.",
